# Shared Exceptions

All domain/infra failures are signalled via exceptions in `LoadlyAggregator.Shared.Exceptions`, which implement `ILocalizedException` (dotted key + args). The global middleware translates them into the right HTTP status + localized message.

## When to throw what

| Situation                                                 | Exception                   | HTTP |
|-----------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------|------|
| Entity not found by id/criteria                           | `NotFoundException`         | 404  |
| Business invariant / validation that FluentValidation can't express | `ValidationException` | 422  |
| Authenticated user is forbidden to touch this resource    | `ForbiddenException`        | 403  |
| No valid authenticated identity / expired token / bad creds | `UnauthorizedException`   | 401  |
| Illegal/inconsistent state that isn't a user input error  | `LogicalException`          | 400  |
| Rate limit / throttling                                   | `TooManyRequestsException`  | 429  |

## How to throw

Always pass a dotted i18n key that exists in both `Messages.en.json` and `Messages.ar.json`, with positional args:

```csharp
var admin = await _adminRepository.GetByIdAsync(id)
    ?? throw new NotFoundException("admins.not_found_with_id", id);

if (contract.Status != ContractStatus.APPROVED)
    throw new ValidationException("contracts.must_be_approved_before_invoicing");

if (!userBelongsToCompany)
    throw new ForbiddenException("auth.cannot_access_other_company_resources");
```

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ `throw new Exception("...")` or `throw new InvalidOperationException("...")` — not translated, wrong status code.
- ❌ Returning an error envelope / `null` instead of throwing.
- ❌ Hardcoded English strings in the exception message — the message **is** the i18n key.
- ❌ Catching one of these in a controller and rewrapping — let the exception middleware handle it.
